Lojban is really different from other languages and trying to directly
compare them can be misleading.

It may be useful at the beginning to grasp the basics, but sooner or later
you have to think in "lojbanic terms".

I think the best way to move forward is to try to translate something into
Lojban. It requires a lot of effort but it makes you explore the language
more and more, until you get it better and better.

